// An unsigned operand in float arithmetic is converted like an integer one.
// It used to be taken as already a float: an unsigned #analog -- the default
// since 2026-10-07 -- times a scale factor came out 65536 times too small.
#analog Vraw:12 in 0:2
#variable U:12 unsigned = 1000
#variable A float = 0.0
#variable V float = 0.0
#variable Lo = 0
A = U * 0.25
V = Vraw * 0.5
Lo = 1 ? Vraw * 0.5 < 1000.0
